uts (not the generator's size-bounded programs)? | `nvim --headless -u NONE -l tools/libdiff.lua <fn> [--n <count>] [--seed <n>] [--js <expr>]` — `cartograph.luajs.libdiff`: a declared input family per function (`FAMILIES[fn](rng, n)`, weighted to the boundaries: tonumber = decimal, hex, long digit runs, exponent limits, whitespace, inf/nan in every case, malformed, embedded NUL), the oracle is this process's LuaJIT, the pack runs under node on the same bytes; results compared by BITS (NaN one class, errors one class); prints the count that DIFFER and the shortest differing inputs. `--js` substitutes the pack side (a JS expression over P, G) to test a candidate or run a POSITIVE CONTROL — a family that never separates a wrong implementation cannot accept a right one (a naive `Number()` tonumber: 5,877 of 20,000 differ). CART-1211, CART-1220 |","after":"| Transliterate C with ARBITRARY GOTOS and wide heap data — e.g. LuaJIT's number formatter lj_strfmt_wfnum behind tostring | `nvim --headless -u NONE -l tools/cjs.lua strfmt <packmap tree src dir> <out.js>` — `cartograph.cjs` exact heap mode, plus: THE GOTO FALLBACK — a function whose gotos the structured forms refuse (into a sibling block, backward into an earlier one, out of an if-chain to a shared tail, into a loop body) is lowered WHOLE to a label-dispatch loop (`$d: for (;;) switch ($L)`: every if/loop/switch/break/continue/goto a numbered jump, so no JS break can mean the wrong construct), locals hoisted with C's block scope kept (a re-declared name gets its own variable), heap locals allocated once at entry — only such functions change form; WIDE heap data: uint16/32/64 and double elements through pointers by DataView (`*p++`, `p[i] +=`, `p += n`, `p - q` scaled by the element width), static tables of any scalar type in the heap image, a named nested member as a PATH (`t.u32.hi`, offsetof from the compiler), `(T)(x)` with a typedef T read as the cast the grammar cannot see, a short as 16 bits of storage. MEASUR